@@ -14,6 +14,10 @@ of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
 - `quote({ itemId, start, end })`: returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`.
 - `book({ itemId, start, end })`: returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`; throws if the item is not
   free for the whole period.
+- `cancel(bookingId, at)`: cancels the booking at the ISO-8601 UTC time `at` and returns
+  `{ bookingId, refund }` in integer cents: the full total when `at` is at least 24 hours before the
+  booking's start, 0 otherwise. The equipment is free again; throws for an unknown booking, an invalid
+  `at`, or a booking already cancelled.
 - `availability({ start, end, kind? })`: returns the sorted ids of the equipment of that kind (any kind
   when `kind` is omitted) that is free for the whole period; throws for an invalid period or unknown kind.
 
@@ -25,7 +29,7 @@ Daily times are ISO-8601 UTC strings (ending in `Z`) at midnight; `end` is the s
 rented day, so `2026-07-01T00:00:00Z` to `2026-07-03T00:00:00Z` is two days. A rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full price (rounded to whole cents); `quote` and
 `book` both return the reduced total. Overlapping bookings of the
 same item are refused; back-to-back ones are fine. Booking ids are sequential (`booking-1`, ...) so the
-service is deterministic. Cancellation (no refund under 24 hours before the start, full refund otherwise)
-is not implemented yet.
+service is deterministic. Cancelled bookings no longer block
+their period, and their ids are never reused.
 
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
